    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d760">

                <pb facs="1043" n="923" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg923"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2781: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-25T12:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 25,
                                1922—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received October 25—6:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>176. Under date of October 24th Count Uchida gave formal consent to proposals
                    contained in your 115, October 13, 7 p.m.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d760-f1"/> The
                    note after accepting our proposals states, “I beg to state in addition that the
                    Japanese Government desire that the points contained in the memorandum which I
                    handed you on October 16 be deemed supplementary to insofar as they can be made
                    compatible with the American proposals above referred to”.</p>
                <p>The memorandum referred to was forwarded in my 172, October 17, 2 p.m. In my 172
                    the date was given as September 16, although it was handed me on October 16th.
                    This was a mistake in the Foreign Office and the memorandum should be referred
                    to as dated October 16th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
